      "jobId": "bffe822c-da94-48cc-9742-5210f9378927",
      "question": "Among declared industry peers, which stocks were the most central in the return-correlation network from December 2025 through March 12, 2026, and which pairs moved together most closely?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-01T04:43:18.148404Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-01T04:43:44.347741Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "**Most central stocks in the declared‑industry return‑correlation network (Dec 2025 – Mar 12 2026)**\n\n| Rank | Ticker | PageRank centrality |\n|------|--------|--------------------|\n| 1 | **BMY** | 0.00809 |\n| 2 | **ABBV** | 0.00728 |\n| 3 | **PFE** | 0.00645 |\n| 4 | **LLY** | 0.00601 |\n| 5 | **MRK** | 0.00601 |\n| 6 | **JNJ** | 0.00590 |\n| 7 | **AZN** | 0.00530 |\n| 8 | **ABT** | 0.00492 |\n| 9 | **COLB** | 0.00361 |\n|10 | **CRWD** | 0.00356 |\n\n*Centrality is computed on the graph whose edges join declared same‑industry peers, weighted by daily‑return correlation over the full window (2025‑12‑01 → 2026‑03‑12). It summarises network position only and does not imply causation.*[1]\n\n---\n\n**Pairs with the strongest absolute return correlation (i.e., moved together most closely)**\n\n| Rank | Ticker 1 | Ticker 2 | Correlation |\n|------|----------|----------|-------------|\n| 1 | **GOOG** | **GOOGL** | **+0.9965** |\n| 2 | **BRK.A** | **BRK.B** | **+0.9891** |\n| 3 | **BYNO** | **CEPO** | **‑0.9764** |\n| 4 | **BF.A** | **BF.B** | **+0.9736** |\n| 5 | **BELFA** | **BELFB** | **+0.9458** |\n| 6 | **BATRA** | **BATRK** | **+0.9230** |\n| 7 | **AUB** | **COLB** | **+0.9057** |\n| 8 | **BEP** | **BEPC** | **+0.9016** |\n| 9 | **CBRE** | **CWK** | **+0.9014** |\n|10 | **GS** | **MS** | **+0.8902** |\n\n*The “strongest edges” are ranked by absolute correlation; a negative value (e.g., BYNO ↔ CEPO) means the two stocks moved in opposite directions almost perfectly.*[1]\n\n---\n\n**Limitations**\n- Centrality and correlation are descriptive network metrics; they do not establish causal relationships.\n- The graph includes all 1,422 assets and 13,248 declared peer edges; only the top‑10 by each metric are shown.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Market analytics result — analyze market relationships — evidence `hermes-receipt:23e225cb4c475a9e1c73a91e19cc47e2b66855a8245cb1e09f1a9b6be2c6f66b`",
